FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** the people who own most of these paths have left, and the only active names here are thin or unconfirmed. Routing needs a decision from you.

**Exposure (`lib/grape_entity/exposure`, 10 files, 609 non-blank lines / 732 with blank lines)**

| Author | Lines (non-blank / with blank) | Commits | Last commit | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Vladimir Kochnev | 331 (54.4%) / 400 | 5 | 2015-09-18 | inactive |
| Marco Silva | 117 (19.2%) / 143, all in `grouped_exposure.rb` | 1 | 2026-08-03 | marked active, but see below |
| Alexander Yunin | 55 / 61 | 2 | 2016-07-04 | inactive |
| James McCarthy | 48 / 58 | 2 | 2017-04-05 | inactive |
| Dmitry Tsepelev | 18 / 22 | 3 | 2018-01-29 | inactive |
| peter scholz | 14 / 18 | 5 | 2024-04-10 | inactive |
| Anna Kowalczyk | 4 / 5 | 1 | 2026-08-10 | active |

Only 2 of 18 authors are active, holding 19.9% of the lines. Marc Rohloff and Andrei Subbota, the two active people in the repo brief, have no commits in this path.

**Delegator code (`lib/grape_entity/delegator.rb`: 24 / 27 lines; `lib/grape_entity/delegators/`: 61 / 69 lines)**

- `delegators/` is almost entirely Vladimir Kochnev's: 47 of 61 lines (77.0%). Nobody with lines there has committed in the last year, and the files were moved in from `lib/grape_entity/delegator/`, so that path has no commit history of its own.
- `delegator.rb`: Vladimir Kochnev 11 / 12 lines (inactive), Paul Padier 6 / 6 (last commit 2021-10-15, inactive), Marco Silva 4 / 4 (active, last commit 2026-07-21). Vladimir Kochnev also owns `exposure/delegator_exposure.rb` (12 lines, 91.7%).

**Who has effectively left:** Vladimir Kochnev, Alexander Yunin, James McCarthy, Dmitry Tsepelev, Paul Padier, and peter scholz. "Inactive" here means no commit in the 365 days before the ref date.

**Caveat on Marco Silva:** SL reports 117 exposure lines under the placeholder address `<email redacted>` and says they "cannot be attributed to a person… not someone to ask." The same name has recent commits, so it is unclear whether this is a real current maintainer. SL proposes merging that address with `marco.silva@kestrel.example`, but I did not apply the merge. Confirm who Marco Silva is before routing to them.

**Recommended routing**

- **Exposure:** Marco Silva if confirmed as a current maintainer (they own `grouped_exposure.rb`, the only recent work). Otherwise Anna Kowalczyk, but with 4 lines that is thin. I did not check whether dblock is active on these paths; `surviving-lines --why-not dblock -- lib/grape_entity/exposure` would answer that.
- **Delegators:** Marco Silva is the only active name with lines here, and only in `delegator.rb`.

**Is the most-commits person also the most-code owner?**

- **Repo-wide: no.** dblock has the most commits (52, 18.2%) but 565 non-blank lines (10.4%). Vladimir Kochnev has the most lines (1,010 non-blank, 18.7%) with 11 commits (3.8%).
- **Exposure: yes on lines, tied on commits.** Vladimir Kochnev has 331 lines and ties peter scholz for most commits (5 each).
- **Delegators: the commit column is not meaningful** here because the files were moved in.

**Caveats**

- Every count above is from surviving-lines. The directory-scoped numbers come from my own runs with path scoping; the repo-wide ones come from the brief.
- Activity is measured against the ref date, 2026-10-05. Today is 2026-10-24, so any commits made after the ref date are not reflected.
- These are survivorship shares, not a measure of who understands the code.

